##
## Kedra Linux repository mirrorlist
##
## Installed as /etc/pacman.d/kedra-mirrorlist and included from the [kedra]
## section of /etc/pacman.conf, mirroring how CachyOS ships its own mirrorlists.
##
## Server lines use pacman's `$repo` and `$arch` variables, so the same line
## works unchanged when publishing moves from a local directory to HTTPS:
##
##     Server = <base>/$repo/os/$arch
##
## No production Kedra mirror exists yet -- no domain has been chosen, and this
## file must not pretend otherwise. The only entry below is the local
## development docroot written by kedra-repo-publish. Replace it (or prepend
## real mirrors above it) once hosting is decided.
##

## Local development repository
Server = file://@KEDRA_REPO_ROOT@/$repo/os/$arch
